I do have a script, but it works only for cutouts. Probably won't do rounded corners (can't test), and trying to improve it to use `DisplayServer.get_display_safe_area()` or `DisplayServer.screen_get_usable_rect()` would require thought on how to deal with window position, and test on multiple devices that I don't have.

I could only test this on Android phones (one normal unobstructed rect and one that has both camera cutout and rounded corners) in a single screen (no external 2nd display), and I've confirmed it works even on a floating window and on side-by-side windows.

